Hi Tristan,

Thanks for sitting down with me at 11:15. On the fifth I noted when you moved=
 to the memo and when everyone first wrote a decision. This morning I timed t=
he explanation from 10:00 to 10:35. That gives us a place to try the two paus=
es we talked about.

Could we put the notice, memo and register on the table and talk through what=
 you=E2=80=99ll ask at each pause? At minute 15, I=E2=80=99d give everyone a =
slip to write the ordinary return time and the words on the notice that give =
it. At minute 30, I=E2=80=99d have each person write down what the applicatio=
n entry and the approval field show before we ask what reception can tell the=
 borrower. Let=E2=80=99s see whether we can leave enough quiet writing time w=
ithin the three minutes at each stop.

I=E2=80=99ve attached my feedback on the two visits and a separate spreadshee=
t so we can put today=E2=80=99s timed blocks beside the proposed 50-minute se=
quence. If I come in again, I=E2=80=99d like to hear which words or entries p=
eople use to explain their decisions.

Thanks,
Heather

